proof.text:
Conjugate the exceptional datum using the comparisons just established. Suppressing the canonical $QG_X\cong G_{X'}Q$ only, Step 1 and $B_EQ(a_f)=a'B_P$ give
$$B_EQ(\varphi_E)G_{X'}(B_E)^{-1}
=a'B_PQ(\varphi_P)G_{X'}(B_P)^{-1}G_{X'}(a')^{-1}
=a'\varphi'_PG_{X'}(a')^{-1}=\varphi'_E.$$
The middle equality is the source-datum equation in Step 8. Hence the exceptional target datum uses precisely the specified base-change identification. The two pasting orders on compact supports agree by Step 8, so the vertical arrows in the compared purity squares also agree.
